From 9c66d2326e9f1d870d78fbc1530614fd2d332004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:16:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/28] generate: STRATA_PIPE_BYIELD_NODRAIN=1 drops a BYIELD
 without draining the pipelined groups

A pipelined read never gives way (batch_read_piece returns 0 when piped), so a
BYIELD that reaches the main loop is for a read that has ended and is dropped.
The main loop still drained the groups for it first, as for a request, unless
STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP was set. With the switch the BYIELD is dropped as it comes.

A BYIELD the server sends during the read is queued and taken right after BADM,
before any group is restarted, so that drain costs nothing today (0 groups in
flight, 0.0 ms). Only a BYIELD that arrives once the groups run again (the
server reads the control lines late) paid for it: measured with one sent 60 ms
after BADM, drain 26 ms with 4 groups in flight and the first rows 50 ms after
it, a 23.5 ms gap in the slots' rows and about 14 rows lost (at 576 rows/s). With
the switch the longest gap is 7.1 ms, as in plain decode.

Off by default: the same path as before. Tokens: batch_overlap_test (a BYIELD
during B's read) on vs off token- and RESUME-identical, batch_interleave_test
output byte-identical, batch_test16 16/16, and 41 sampled requests of the
admission driver (8 with a BYIELD while 4 groups were in flight) equal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/program/generate.cpp | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/program/generate.cpp b/src/program/generate.cpp
index 843e27de..7c987337 100644
--- a/src/program/generate.cpp
+++ b/src/program/generate.cpp
@@ -166,6 +166,16 @@ bool pipe_overlap_env() {
     }();
     return on;
 }
+// STRATA_PIPE_BYIELD_NODRAIN=1 (read once; off by default): with the pipelined groups, a BYIELD that reaches the main
+// loop is dropped without draining the groups first.  A pipelined read never gives way (batch_read_piece), so the
+// BYIELD is for a read that has ended, and the drain (and the refill after it) did nothing for it
+bool pipe_byield_nodrain_env() {
+    static const bool on = [] {
+        const char* v = std::getenv("STRATA_PIPE_BYIELD_NODRAIN");
+        return v && v[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    return on;
+}
 // STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP's debug knobs (tests only; unset: 0, nothing changes).  STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_FORCE_PADUP=1: a group
 // started during an overlapped read always runs padded up (a wider layout whose extra rows park no conversation, else
 // it waits).  STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_FORCE_WAIT=1: never padded up, a group whose own layout is missing waits for the
@@ -9779,9 +9789,10 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
                     }
                     ov_dec_valid = false;
                 }
-                // a request reads its prompt through every stage: the groups in flight finish first (STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP:
-                // not for a BYIELD, which is dropped below)
-                if (piped && line.rfind("BSTOP ", 0) != 0 && !(pipe_overlap_env() && line.rfind("BYIELD", 0) == 0)) {
+                // a request reads its prompt through every stage: the groups in flight finish first (STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP,
+                // STRATA_PIPE_BYIELD_NODRAIN: not for a BYIELD, which is dropped below)
+                if (piped && line.rfind("BSTOP ", 0) != 0 &&
+                    !((pipe_overlap_env() || pipe_byield_nodrain_env()) && line.rfind("BYIELD", 0) == 0)) {
                     const int in_flight = trace ? (int) std::count_if(pg.begin(), pg.end(), [](const PGroup& G) {
                                                       return G.inflight; }) : 0;
                     const auto td = Clock::now();
